.TH SAMBA 8 "2026-10-05" "samba" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
samba \- pure-Go SMB2/SMB3 file server (zero-copy reads, multichannel)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B samba
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-\-check\fR]
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B samba
is a from-scratch SMB2/3 file server, an
.BR smbd (8)
replacement, written entirely in Go: no CGO, no \f(CWunsafe\fR. It listens on
TCP 445 only (direct TCP; there is no NetBIOS port 139, no RPC, and no
management API), and it serves every worker from its own
.BR SO_REUSEPORT
listener so the kernel spreads connections across CPU cores.
.PP
It speaks SMB 2.0.2 through 3.1.1 with NTLMv2 and Kerberos (GSS-API/SPNEGO)
authentication, SMB2/3 signing, SMB 3.1.1 preauth integrity, SMB3 multichannel,
SMB3 encryption (AES-128/256-GCM and AES-128/256-CCM), byte-range locks,
directory change notification, and read- and handle-caching leases.
.PP
Large unsigned reads never copy the file's data through userspace: the response
header is written and the kernel moves page-cache pages straight into the socket
with
.BR splice (2).
Reads that must be signed or encrypted, and reads inside a compound request,
take a buffered positional-read path instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIpath\fR " (or " \-c ")"
Path to the TOML configuration file. Default: \fIsamba.toml\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Validate the configuration and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-version " (or " \-V ")"
Print the version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is TOML, by convention \fI/etc/samba/samba.toml\fR. Unknown keys
are rejected. See
.I samba.toml.example
for a fully commented file.
.TP
.B listen
Bind address, default \fB"0.0.0.0:445"\fR. Binding 445 needs
CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE or root.
.TP
.B workers
Listener goroutines, each with its own SO_REUSEPORT listener. 0 = one per CPU
core.
.TP
.B server_name
Advertised server name; also the default Kerberos SPN host (\fIcifs/<name>\fR).
.TP
.B log_level
0 = warn, 1 = info, 2 = debug.
.TP
.B allow_guest
Allow unauthenticated guest sessions. Defaults to true only when no
\fB[[user]]\fR entries exist.
.TP
.B require_signing
Reject unsigned requests on authenticated sessions.
.TP
.B encrypt
Require SMB3 encryption on all post-authentication traffic. Default false;
encryption a client asks for (e.g. cifs \fBseal\fR) is honored either way.
.TP
.B prefer_aes256
Prefer AES-256 (GCM, then CCM) when the client offers it, instead of honoring
the client's preference order.
.TP
.B multichannel
Advertise SMB3 multichannel and accept session binding.
.TP
.B advertise_only
Addresses to advertise for multichannel (e.g. a dedicated storage NIC). Empty =
every non-loopback interface.
.TP
.B oplocks
Grant leases: read-caching, plus handle-caching when the client asks. Default
true. Write-caching is never granted.
.TP
.B auth
\fB"ntlm"\fR, \fB"kerberos"\fR or \fB"both"\fR (the default; Kerberos is
preferred with NTLM as fallback).
.TP
.B [kerberos]
\fBenabled\fR (default true), \fBkeytab\fR (default
\fI$KRB5_KTNAME\fR, then \fI/etc/krb5.keytab\fR), \fBspn\fR (default
\fIcifs/<server_name>\fR) and \fBrealm\fR (parsed; the realm actually comes from
the ticket).
.TP
.B [[share]]
At least one is required: \fBname\fR, \fBpath\fR (an existing directory) and
\fBread_only\fR (default false). The name \fIIPC$\fR is reserved.
.TP
.B [[user]]
\fBname\fR plus exactly one of \fBpassword\fR or \fBnt_hash\fR (32 hex
characters). NTLM users only; Kerberos principals come from the KDC.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/samba/samba.toml
Conventional configuration path.
.TP
.I samba.toml
Default when \fB\-\-config\fR is not given.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
# /etc/samba/samba.toml
listen = "0.0.0.0:445"
require_signing = true
multichannel = true

[[share]]
name = "data"
path = "/srv/data"

[[user]]
name = "alice"
password = "secret"
.fi
.PP
Run it:
.PP
.nf
samba --config /etc/samba/samba.toml
.fi
.PP
Mount it from a client:
.PP
.nf
mount -t cifs //server/data /mnt -o username=alice,password=secret,vers=3.1.1,sec=ntlmsspi
mount -t cifs //server/data /mnt -o username=alice,password=secret,vers=3.1.1,seal
mount -t cifs //server/data /mnt -o username=alice,password=secret,vers=3.1.1,multichannel,max_channels=4
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean shutdown.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error, a configuration error, or a startup failure.
.SH SECURITY
Authorization is \fBshare-level only\fR: \fBread_only\fR applies to every user,
and all file I/O runs as the server's Unix user. Run the server as a dedicated
unprivileged user that owns only the share trees. No external security review has
been done; do not expose port 445 to the public internet. See
.I SECURITY.md.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smbd (8),
.BR mount.cifs (8),
.BR docs/ARCHITECTURE.md ,
.BR docs/TUNING.md
